From 89f78683f25aec401f5840aef0f2aee6e8b20e7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:03:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(import): a STEP import reports the chord error of the
 mesh it kept

The refinement schedule moves to step_refine::refine, which returns the
kept mesh with its own chord tolerance: a pass dropped for crossing the
facet budget no longer leaves the halved tolerance on the coarser mesh
(the log under-reported the error, and said nothing when the halved
value hit the target). step::parse_with_chord returns the mesh and the
coarsest kept tolerance in mm, refusing a non-finite or negative value;
step::parse is unchanged (same schedule, same meshes). A thread-local
test-only budget override forces a small fixture over budget.

Held work: the UI/MCP flag and the law tightening are escalated to
effort:max on the issue.

Refs #864

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
